thmap: concurrent trie-hash map, used by NPF (connection and table maps).

Upstream:	https://github.com/rmind/thmap
Imported:	commit b8ade06 (2023-10-30); dist/ is upstream's src/.
License:	BSD-2-Clause (dist/LICENSE).

Local changes (MINIX):
- dist/utils.h: SPINLOCK_BACKOFF() calls sched_yield() once the back-off
  is at its maximum, in programs (not in system services).  On MINIX a
  node-lock holder can be waiting for the CPU its waiter spins on, and a
  pure spin then burns a whole quantum: thmap_stress on two CPUs took
  ~20 minutes instead of ~10 seconds.

Built and run by minix/tests/npfdeps (t_thmap, thmap_stress).

To update: copy upstream src/ over dist/, then re-apply the change above.
